Here's my latest stoopid "death". I'd finally gotten to exp level 14 and
was heading back upstairs for my quest. I stopped by an altar and decided
to use my wand of create monster and make a few offerings to my god. One of
the first monsters created was a floating eye. Great! A gremlin had stolen
most of my intrinsics, so here was a chance to get one back. I put on my
blindfold (item "Q") and killed it. I then proceeded to remove my blindfold
(item "Q"), move "northwest", and eat the leftover corpse.

Before I realized it, it was asking me if I wanted my posessions identified.

That's when I did a Homer Simpson - D'oh!!! I thought I was wearing an amulet,
but since I was only wearing the blindfold, it automatically removed it (no
need to answer "Q"). Because I thought it would ask me what I wanted to remove,
I had already typed "Q" which the game interpreted as "quit". "Really quit?"
But, I had already moved northwest (i.e., "7", the same as "y"), which answered
that question.

Well, there's one Sunday wasted...

Anyway, these two features (the game interpreting a move northwest as a "yes"
answer, and automatic removal of only item) have stung me quite a few times:

 Hmm. I think I'll head	northwest. 7-7-7-7.

